{
  "_comment": "Canned GitHub responses for the offline scan tests. The Python scanner was served them when expected.json was recorded; scanner.test.ts serves them to lib/scanner. A route is a response or a list of responses given in turn (the last repeats). status 0 is a network failure. Unlisted URLs get a 404. The fixes and admin-denied scenarios were added with 0.3.0, for the focused tests of its bug fixes. The oss-scanner-* scenarios (and the anthropics/oss-scanner routes in public) were added with 0.4.0, for the OSS Scanner check. The private-large scenarios were added with 0.4.1: a private repo big enough for every program lookup, whose Scorecard, Best Practices badge, OSS-Fuzz and OSS Scanner routes answer as if it were enrolled, and the same repo made public. Since 0.4.1 a private repo's scan never requests those routes (admin-org's included). The admin-org, assume-admin and admin-denied scenarios got security advisory routes with 0.5.2: admin-org has an admin's classic token (its scopes in X-OAuth-Scopes), assume-admin an app installation that has accepted the Secrets and Repository security advisories permissions (options.grants), and admin-denied one that hasn't. The public scenario's incident response plan dates a drill.",
